0..75 Comment "// A presented type whose constructor holds a continuation (#2511). A field"
76..142 Comment "// written `A => T` is the description code\'s function former, the"
143..220 Comment "// higher-order descriptions\' `Π` over a type of arguments (Chapman, Dagand,"
221..286 Comment "// McBride and Morris, _The Gentle Art of Levitation_, ICFP 2010,"
287..362 Comment "// doi:10.1145/1863543.1863547). It decodes to the thunked arrow the native"
363..442 Comment "// reading gives the same field, so the type keeps its rule. Programs that read"
443..519 Comment "// and store a state are state\'s free model, and put-put is the law of state"
520..590 Comment "// a store obeys (Plotkin and Power, _Notions of computation determine"
591..639 Comment "// monads_, 2002, doi:10.1007/3-540-45931-6_24)."
641..706 Comment "/// Programs over an integer state: a read hands the state to its"
707..775 Comment "/// continuation, and a store the next store overwrites is no store."
